--
Multi-argument std::function construction and call (C++11).  Now fully works:
construction resolves and wires up the handler pointers, operator() forwards all
arguments, and the _M_invoke/__invoke_r dispatch returns the correct result.  The
final root was the explicit-leading-template-argument + deduced-trailing-pack
instantiation over-expanding the function parameter pack by one
(cpp11_explicit_targ_deduced_trailing_pack); fixed in
cpp_typecheck_resolvet::resolve.  Earlier layers: partial-spec pack deduction
(cpp11_partial_spec_pack_after_fixed), member function-pointer pack arity
(cpp11_variadic_pack_in_member_funptr_type / _primary), and method-body pack
expansion (cpp11_variadic_pack_in_method_body_call).  N5008 [func.wrap.func],
[temp.variadic]/5, [temp.deduct.call]/3.  Non-vacuous (assertion 2 must FAIL).
